WEBVTT

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:16.933
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off --

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:21.000
Saving people, hunting things,
the family business.

00:00:23.338 --> 00:00:26.305
You know the truth
about sammy.

00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:28.839
I've known for a while.

00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:32.038
You get premonitions
of people about to die?

00:00:33.172 --> 00:00:34.138
Death visions?

00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:35.338
Yeah.

00:00:35.372 --> 00:00:37.806
Sam: the demon
said he had plans for me.

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:40.305
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:00:40.338 --> 00:00:42.005
No.

00:00:42.038 --> 00:00:45.038
I want you to watch out
for sammy, okay?

00:00:45.071 --> 00:00:47.372
Did he say anything
to you?

00:00:47.405 --> 00:00:49.372
No.

00:00:50.672 --> 00:00:52.238
I can't talk about this
to sammy.

00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:54.238
I've got to keep
my game face on.

00:00:54.272 --> 00:00:56.906
You're erratic,
except for when you're hunting.

00:00:56.971 --> 00:00:58.705
'Cause then,
you're downright scary.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:02.038
The truth is,
i'm not handling it very well.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:07.205
You're tailspinning, man,
and you won't let me help you.

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:38.772
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:41.439
No, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:43.971
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:01:44.005 --> 00:01:45.439
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.372
He's not him --
Not anymore.

00:01:47.405 --> 00:01:50.105
Stop it! Ask her!
Ask the doctor!

00:01:50.138 --> 00:01:51.605
It's not in me!

00:01:51.639 --> 00:01:53.205
I...just...

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:55.772
i can't tell.

00:01:55.806 --> 00:01:58.238
No, please, don't.
Don't.

00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:00.971
I've got no choice.

00:02:01.005 --> 00:02:03.605
It's not in me.

00:02:25.038 --> 00:02:26.305
Sam?

00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:33.064
<Font color="#ffff00">www.1000fr.Com present</font>

00:02:33.064 --> 00:02:38.027
uploaded for opensubtitles.org by najic (",)

00:02:41.347 --> 00:02:44.070
<i>Woman:
continue on or-224 west.</i>

00:02:44.071 --> 00:02:46.572
There are only two towns
in the u.S. Named rivergrove.

00:02:46.605 --> 00:02:49.272
How come you're so sure
it's the one in oregon?

00:02:50.605 --> 00:02:53.705
There was a picture.

00:02:55.772 --> 00:02:57.405
Okay, what else?

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:02.605
I saw a dark room, some people,
and a guy tied to a chair.

00:03:02.639 --> 00:03:04.439
And i ventilated him?

00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:08.172
Yeah. You thought there was
something inside him.

00:03:08.205 --> 00:03:11.736
A demon? Was he possessed?

00:03:11.736 --> 00:03:12.071
All your weirdo visions

00:03:12.105 --> 00:03:13.938
Are always tied to
the yellow-Eyed demon.

00:03:13.971 --> 00:03:16.739
Was there any black smoke?
Did we try to exorcise him?

00:03:16.772 --> 00:03:19.672
No. Nothing.
You just plugged him.

00:03:19.705 --> 00:03:20.672
That's it.

00:03:20.705 --> 00:03:22.439
Well, i'm sure
i had a good reason.

00:03:22.472 --> 00:03:24.439
I sure hope so.

00:03:26.725 --> 00:03:29.491
What does that mean?

00:03:30.724 --> 00:03:33.958
I'm not gonna
waste an innocent man.

00:03:34.256 --> 00:03:35.855
I wouldn't.
I never said you would.

00:03:35.889 --> 00:03:37.289
Fine.
Fine.

00:03:37.322 --> 00:03:38.922
Look, we don't
know what it is.

00:03:38.955 --> 00:03:41.623
But whatever it is, that guy
in the chair is a part of it.

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:43.623
So, let's find him
and see what's what.

00:03:43.688 --> 00:03:45.222
Fine.
Fine.

00:04:28.855 --> 00:04:30.189
He was there.

00:04:33.955 --> 00:04:34.922
Morning.

00:04:34.955 --> 00:04:37.222
Morning.
Can i help you?

00:04:37.256 --> 00:04:40.122
Yeah. Billy gibbons,
frank beard.

00:04:40.156 --> 00:04:41.556
U.S. Marshals.

00:04:41.589 --> 00:04:43.422
What's this about?

00:04:43.456 --> 00:04:44.456
We're looking for someone.

00:04:44.489 --> 00:04:47.289
A young man, early 20s.

00:04:47.322 --> 00:04:52.156
He'd have a thin scar
right below his hairline.

00:04:52.189 --> 00:04:54.089
What did he do?

00:04:54.122 --> 00:04:55.688
We're actually
looking for someone else,

00:04:55.722 --> 00:04:57.855
But we think
this young man can help us.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:00.556
He's not in any kind of trouble
or anything. Not yet.

00:05:04.322 --> 00:05:07.955
I think maybe you
know who he is, master sergeant.

00:05:07.989 --> 00:05:11.122
My dad was in the corps.
He was a corporal.

00:05:11.156 --> 00:05:12.122
What company?

00:05:12.156 --> 00:05:13.456
Echo-2-1.

00:05:13.489 --> 00:05:14.889
So, can you help us?

00:05:17.655 --> 00:05:21.623
Duane tanner's
got a scar like that.

00:05:21.655 --> 00:05:23.389
But i know him.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.422
Good kid.
Keeps his nose clean.

00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:28.289
Oh, i'm sure he does.
Do you know where he lives?

00:05:28.322 --> 00:05:33.456
With his family,
up aspen way.

00:05:33.489 --> 00:05:34.456
Thank you.

00:05:34.489 --> 00:05:36.489
Thanks.

00:05:48.623 --> 00:05:50.489
Hey.

00:05:58.256 --> 00:05:59.655
"Croatoan"?

00:05:59.688 --> 00:06:00.788
Yeah.

00:06:01.922 --> 00:06:04.989
Roanoke. Lost colony.
Ring a bell?

00:06:05.022 --> 00:06:08.322
Dean, did you pay any attention
to history class?

00:06:08.356 --> 00:06:11.289
Yeah. The shot heard
around the world.

00:06:11.322 --> 00:06:12.989
How bills become laws.

00:06:13.022 --> 00:06:16.422
That's not school.
That's "schoolhouse rock."

00:06:17.855 --> 00:06:18.822
Whatever.

00:06:18.855 --> 00:06:20.788
Roanoke was one
of the first

00:06:20.822 --> 00:06:23.523
English colonies in america --
Late 1500s.

00:06:23.556 --> 00:06:25.556
Oh, yeah, yeah,
i do remember that.

00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:27.389
The only thing
they left behind

00:06:27.422 --> 00:06:29.889
Was a single word carved
in a tree.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.156
"Croatoan."

00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:33.122
Yeah, and there were
theories --

00:06:33.156 --> 00:06:34.222
Indian raid, disease --

00:06:34.256 --> 00:06:35.822
But nobody knows
what really happened.

00:06:35.855 --> 00:06:39.489
They were all just gone,
wiped out overnight.

00:06:39.523 --> 00:06:43.422
You don't think
that's what's going on here.

00:06:43.456 --> 00:06:45.889
Whatever i saw in my head,
it sure wasn't good.

00:06:48.356 --> 00:06:49.989
But what do you think
could do that?

00:06:53.855 --> 00:06:56.489
Well, i mean, like i said,
all your weirdo visions

00:06:56.523 --> 00:06:59.489
Are always tied to the
yellow-Eyed demon somehow, so...

00:06:59.523 --> 00:07:02.156
we should get help.

00:07:02.189 --> 00:07:04.389
Bobby. Ellen, maybe.

00:07:04.422 --> 00:07:06.456
Yeah,
that's a good idea.

00:07:11.456 --> 00:07:13.623
I don't have a signal.

00:07:19.456 --> 00:07:21.623
I don't either.

00:07:31.722 --> 00:07:35.022
The line's dead.

00:07:35.055 --> 00:07:36.688
I'll tell you one thing --

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.589
If i was gonna
massacre a town,

00:07:38.623 --> 00:07:41.222
That'd be my first step.

00:07:58.822 --> 00:08:00.556
Yeah?

00:08:00.589 --> 00:08:03.122
Hi, looking for duane tanner.
He lives here, right?

00:08:03.156 --> 00:08:05.389
He's my brother.

00:08:05.422 --> 00:08:06.989
Can we talk to him?

00:08:07.022 --> 00:08:09.089
He's not here right now.

00:08:09.122 --> 00:08:10.322
Do you know where he is?

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:13.523
Yeah, he went on a fishing trip
up by roslyn lake.

00:08:13.556 --> 00:08:15.356
Your parents home?
Yeah, they're inside.

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:16.389
Man:
jake, who is it?

00:08:18.022 --> 00:08:20.655
Dean:
hi, u.S. Marshals, sir.

00:08:20.688 --> 00:08:23.322
We're looking
for your son duane.

00:08:23.356 --> 00:08:24.655
He's not in trouble,
is he?

00:08:24.688 --> 00:08:27.322
We just need to ask him
a couple routine questions.

00:08:27.356 --> 00:08:29.489
When is he due back
from his trip?

00:08:29.523 --> 00:08:31.055
I'm not sure.

00:08:31.089 --> 00:08:34.256
Well,
maybe your wife knows.

00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:36.755
No, i don't know.
She's not here right now.

00:08:36.788 --> 00:08:38.156
Well,
your son said she was.

00:08:38.189 --> 00:08:39.222
Did i?

00:08:39.256 --> 00:08:42.022
She's getting groceries.

00:08:42.055 --> 00:08:43.922
So, when duane gets back,

00:08:43.955 --> 00:08:46.156
There's a number
where he can get ahold of you?

00:08:46.189 --> 00:08:48.489
Oh, no, we'll just check in
with you later.

00:08:53.889 --> 00:08:56.356
That was kind of creepy,
right?

00:08:56.389 --> 00:08:57.688
A little too stepford?

00:08:57.722 --> 00:08:59.556
Big-Time.

00:09:09.822 --> 00:09:14.156
It's okay, mom.
It's not gonna hurt.

00:09:34.389 --> 00:09:35.822
Put it down!

00:10:13.768 --> 00:10:16.235
Hello?

00:10:16.268 --> 00:10:18.601
Hello?
We need a doctor here.

00:10:20.263 --> 00:10:22.064
Mrs. Tanner,
what happened?

00:10:22.097 --> 00:10:23.230
She's been attacked.

00:10:23.263 --> 00:10:24.263
Dr. Lee?

00:10:27.363 --> 00:10:28.330
It's okay.

00:10:28.363 --> 00:10:30.064
Bring her in.

00:10:30.097 --> 00:10:31.263
Okay.

00:10:33.196 --> 00:10:35.163
Hey.

00:10:35.196 --> 00:10:37.864
Is that...?

00:10:39.263 --> 00:10:40.664
Mr. Tanner?

00:10:40.697 --> 00:10:42.664
Was he attacked, too?

00:10:42.697 --> 00:10:44.964
Uh, no, actually,
he did the attacking,

00:10:44.997 --> 00:10:46.797
And then
he got himself shot.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.163
Shot?
Yeah.

00:10:48.196 --> 00:10:49.397
And who are you?

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.563
U.S. Marshal.
I'd show you my badge, but...

00:10:52.597 --> 00:10:55.196
oh, sorry.
Bring him back here.

00:10:57.363 --> 00:10:59.497
Wait, you said jake
helped him?

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.330
Your son jake?

00:11:01.363 --> 00:11:03.563
They beat me.

00:11:05.296 --> 00:11:07.230
Tied me up.

00:11:07.263 --> 00:11:10.196
I don't believe it.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.530
Pam.

00:11:11.563 --> 00:11:13.697
Beverly,
do you have any idea

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.296
Why they would act
this way?

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.230
Any history
of chemical dependency?

00:11:17.263 --> 00:11:19.563
No, of course not.

00:11:19.597 --> 00:11:21.530
I don't know why.

00:11:21.563 --> 00:11:26.230
One minute,
they were my husband and my son,

00:11:26.263 --> 00:11:30.597
And the next,
they had the devil in them.

00:11:33.296 --> 00:11:35.131
We've got to talk.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.463
Those guys were whacked
out of their gourds.

00:11:43.497 --> 00:11:45.363
What do you think,
mass possession?

00:11:45.397 --> 00:11:47.864
If it is a possession,
there could be more.

00:11:47.897 --> 00:11:49.031
God knows how many.

00:11:49.064 --> 00:11:51.131
It could be like
a freaking shriner convention.

00:11:51.163 --> 00:11:55.061
Of course, that's one way
to wipe out a town --

00:11:55.061 --> 00:11:55.764
You take it
from the inside.

00:11:55.797 --> 00:11:58.430
We didn't see any
of the demon smoke with tanner

00:11:58.463 --> 00:11:59.982
Or any
of the other usual signs.

00:11:59.982 --> 00:12:03.296
Something turned him
into a monster.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.237
You know, if you would have
taken out the other one,

00:12:06.237 --> 00:12:07.824
There would be one less
to worry about.

00:12:07.824 --> 00:12:10.011
I'm sorry.
I hesitated.

00:12:10.012 --> 00:12:11.079
It was a kid.

00:12:11.113 --> 00:12:12.345
No, it was an "it."

00:12:12.378 --> 00:12:15.979
It's not the best time
for a bleeding heart, sam.

00:12:16.012 --> 00:12:17.312
How's the patient?

00:12:17.345 --> 00:12:19.312
Terrible. What the hell
happened out there?

00:12:19.345 --> 00:12:21.312
You just killed
my next-Door neighbor.

00:12:21.345 --> 00:12:22.479
We didn't have a choice.

00:12:22.512 --> 00:12:25.395
Maybe so,
but we need the county sheriff.

00:12:25.395 --> 00:12:26.236
The phones are down.

00:12:26.236 --> 00:12:28.770
I know. I tried. Tell me
you've got a police radio.

00:12:28.803 --> 00:12:31.737
Yeah, we do, but it crapped out
just like everything else.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.770
I don't understand
what is happening.

00:12:33.803 --> 00:12:34.937
How far is it
to the next town?

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.903
It's about 40 miles down
to sidewinder.

00:12:36.937 --> 00:12:39.168
I'm gonna go down there
and see if i can find some help.

00:12:39.169 --> 00:12:41.969
My partner will stick around
and keep you guys safe.

00:12:42.002 --> 00:12:43.735
Safe from what?

00:12:45.802 --> 00:12:48.136
We'll get back to you
on that.

00:14:09.735 --> 00:14:12.069
Huh.

00:14:14.169 --> 00:14:15.303
What?

00:14:15.336 --> 00:14:18.468
His lymphocyte percentage
is pretty high.

00:14:18.502 --> 00:14:21.136
His body was fighting off
a viral infection.

00:14:21.169 --> 00:14:23.735
Really?
What kind of virus?

00:14:23.769 --> 00:14:25.502
I can't say for sure.

00:14:25.535 --> 00:14:28.017
An infection could have made him
act like that?

00:14:28.018 --> 00:14:32.589
Some can cause dementia,
but not that kind of violence.

00:14:32.589 --> 00:14:33.923
And besides,

00:14:33.923 --> 00:14:35.901
I've never heard of one
that did this to the blood.

00:14:35.901 --> 00:14:36.821
Did what?

00:14:36.821 --> 00:14:38.668
There's
this weird residue.

00:14:39.554 --> 00:14:42.920
If i didn't know better,
i'd say it was sulfur.

00:14:49.487 --> 00:14:51.154
Sulfur.

00:15:25.053 --> 00:15:26.788
Oh, ho, ho. Hey.

00:15:26.821 --> 00:15:28.454
Sorry. Road's closed.

00:15:28.487 --> 00:15:30.621
Yeah, i can see that.
What's up?

00:15:30.654 --> 00:15:31.788
Quarantine.

00:15:31.821 --> 00:15:34.120
Quarantine?
What is it?

00:15:34.154 --> 00:15:35.454
Don't know.

00:15:35.487 --> 00:15:37.287
Something going around
out there.

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.120
Uh-Huh.
Who told you that?

00:15:39.154 --> 00:15:40.454
County sheriff.

00:15:40.487 --> 00:15:41.920
Is he here?

00:15:41.953 --> 00:15:44.354
No. He called.

00:15:44.387 --> 00:15:46.053
Say, why don't
you get out of the car,

00:15:46.087 --> 00:15:47.454
And we'll talk a little?

00:15:47.487 --> 00:15:49.854
Well,
you are a handsome devil,

00:15:49.888 --> 00:15:52.421
But i don't swing that way,
sorry.

00:15:52.454 --> 00:15:54.654
I'd sure appreciate it
if you got out of the car,

00:15:54.687 --> 00:15:55.788
Just for a quick minute.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.053
Yeah, i bet you would.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.920
Stop!

00:16:03.953 --> 00:16:05.053
Stop!

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:21.554
I don't understand.

00:16:21.587 --> 00:16:25.888
Are you saying my husband
and jake had a disease?

00:16:25.953 --> 00:16:28.120
That's what
we're trying to find out.

00:16:28.154 --> 00:16:32.120
Now, during the attack,
do you remember --

00:16:32.154 --> 00:16:35.987
Did you have any direct contact
with their blood?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.254
Oh, my god.

00:16:37.287 --> 00:16:40.621
You don't think
i've got this virus, do you?

00:16:40.654 --> 00:16:43.087
Beverly, i don't know
what to think,

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:46.454
But with your permission,
we'll take a blood sample.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:57.421
Aah!

00:16:58.187 --> 00:16:59.320
Aah!

00:17:04.487 --> 00:17:05.821
Aah!

00:17:18.421 --> 00:17:19.721
Hands where
i can see them!

00:17:19.754 --> 00:17:21.053
Son of a --

00:17:21.087 --> 00:17:22.953
Get out of the car!

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:25.521
Out of the car!

00:17:25.554 --> 00:17:28.020
Crap.

00:17:28.053 --> 00:17:30.120
All right.
Easy there, big guy.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:35.421
Put it down!
Lower it now!

00:17:35.454 --> 00:17:36.421
Are you one of them?!

00:17:36.454 --> 00:17:37.421
No, are you?!
No!

00:17:37.454 --> 00:17:39.920
You could be lying!
So could you!

00:17:39.953 --> 00:17:42.053
We could do this all day.
All right.

00:17:42.087 --> 00:17:44.854
Let's just take it easy
before we kill each other.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.987
What's going on
with everybody?

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:50.987
I don't know.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.087
My neighbor, mr. Rogers --

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.087
You've got a neighbor
named mr. Rogers?

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:56.320
Not anymore.

00:17:56.354 --> 00:18:00.320
He came at me with a hatchet.
I put him down.

00:18:00.354 --> 00:18:01.821
He's not the only one.

00:18:01.854 --> 00:18:04.254
I mean, it's happening
to everyone.

00:18:04.287 --> 00:18:05.421
I'm heading to doc's place.

00:18:05.454 --> 00:18:06.920
There's still
some people left.

00:18:06.953 --> 00:18:08.120
I'm getting the hell out.

00:18:08.154 --> 00:18:10.287
There's no way out.
They got the bridge covered.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.754
I don't believe you.
Fine, stay here.
Be my guest.

00:18:29.287 --> 00:18:32.120
Well, this ought to be
a relaxing drive.

00:18:38.487 --> 00:18:41.154
What if we all have it?

00:18:41.187 --> 00:18:43.987
What if we all go crazy?

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.120
You've got to stay calm.
All we can do is wait.

00:18:46.154 --> 00:18:47.621
The marshal
is bringing help.

00:18:47.654 --> 00:18:50.721
I can't.
I've got to go.

00:18:50.754 --> 00:18:52.053
Pam?

00:18:52.087 --> 00:18:54.987
No, you don't understand.
My boyfriend's out there.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.621
I've got to make sure
he's okay.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:04.220
Hey, hey, hey, wait.
Wait, please.

00:19:04.254 --> 00:19:07.254
Look, i know you're upset,
all right.

00:19:07.287 --> 00:19:09.287
But it's safer
if you stay here for now.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.287
Help is coming.

00:19:15.621 --> 00:19:17.953
There they are.

00:19:19.404 --> 00:19:21.383
??

00:19:27.888 --> 00:19:30.854
Did you guys
get to a phone?

00:19:30.888 --> 00:19:32.187
Roadblock.

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:33.854
I'm gonna have a word.
Doc's inside.

00:19:33.888 --> 00:19:36.220
All right.

00:19:36.254 --> 00:19:37.920
What's going on
out there, dean?

00:19:37.953 --> 00:19:40.019
I feel like chuck heston
in "the omega man."

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.948
Sarge is the only sane person
i could find.

00:19:42.948 --> 00:19:44.689
What are we dealing with?
Do you know?

00:19:44.689 --> 00:19:45.989
Yeah,
doc thinks it's a virus.

00:19:46.022 --> 00:19:48.188
Okay, great.
What do you think?

00:19:48.221 --> 00:19:49.555
I think she's right.

00:19:49.589 --> 00:19:51.121
And i think the infected

00:19:51.155 --> 00:19:53.376
Are trying to infect others
with blood-To-Blood contact.

00:19:53.376 --> 00:19:56.708
The virus leaves traces
of sulfur in the blood.

00:19:56.709 --> 00:20:00.473
A demonic virus?
More like demonic
germ warfare.

00:20:01.739 --> 00:20:03.527
At least it explains
why i've been having visions.

00:20:04.572 --> 00:20:06.152
It's like
a biblical plague.

00:20:06.152 --> 00:20:09.286
Yeah. You don't know
how right you are, dean.

00:20:09.319 --> 00:20:11.620
I've been pouring
through dad's journal.

00:20:11.653 --> 00:20:14.119
I found something
about the roanoke colony.

00:20:14.152 --> 00:20:16.653
Dad always had a theory
about "croatoan."

00:20:16.686 --> 00:20:18.286
He thought
it was a demon's name --

00:20:18.319 --> 00:20:19.987
Sometimes known as daeva
or reshef --

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:22.486
A demon of plague
and pestilence.

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:25.419
Well, that's terrific.
Why here? Why now?

00:20:25.453 --> 00:20:26.753
I have no idea.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.286
But, dean, who knows
how far this thing can spread?

00:20:31.319 --> 00:20:33.520
We've got to get out of here.
We've got to warn people.

00:20:33.553 --> 00:20:35.620
Mark: they've got one.
In here.

00:20:37.953 --> 00:20:39.086
What do you mean?

00:20:39.119 --> 00:20:40.620
The wife --
She's infected.

00:20:40.653 --> 00:20:42.353
We've got to take care
of this.

00:20:42.386 --> 00:20:44.019
We can't just leave her
in there.

00:20:44.052 --> 00:20:45.853
My neighbors --
They were strong.

00:20:45.887 --> 00:20:48.152
The longer we wait,
the stronger she'll get.

00:20:54.586 --> 00:20:56.553
You're gonna kill
beverly tanner?

00:20:56.586 --> 00:20:58.953
Doctor, could there
be any treatment?

00:20:58.987 --> 00:21:01.119
Some kind of cure
for this?

00:21:03.353 --> 00:21:04.853
Can you cure it?

00:21:04.887 --> 00:21:06.520
I don't even know
what "it" is.

00:21:06.553 --> 00:21:09.520
It's a matter of time
before she breaks through.

00:21:09.553 --> 00:21:11.353
You can't shoot her
like an animal.

00:21:11.386 --> 00:21:13.953
Sam.

00:21:31.586 --> 00:21:35.319
Mark.
What are you doing?

00:21:35.353 --> 00:21:38.753
Mark, it's them.

00:21:38.786 --> 00:21:42.186
They locked me in here.
They tried to kill me.

00:21:42.219 --> 00:21:44.319
They're infected,
not me.

00:21:44.353 --> 00:21:47.253
Please, mark.

00:21:47.286 --> 00:21:49.820
You've known me
all your life.

00:21:49.853 --> 00:21:53.019
Please.

00:21:53.052 --> 00:21:55.386
Are you sure
she's one of them?

00:21:57.052 --> 00:21:58.887
Yeah.

00:22:50.905 --> 00:22:53.206
Oh, god! Is there any on me?!
Am i okay?!

00:22:53.239 --> 00:22:54.506
You're clean.
You're okay.

00:22:54.539 --> 00:22:57.939
Why are we staying here?
Please, let's just go.

00:22:57.972 --> 00:23:00.106
We can't, 'cause those things
are everywhere.

00:23:00.139 --> 00:23:01.539
Oh, god.
Why is this happening?

00:23:01.573 --> 00:23:04.372
Shh, shh, shh.

00:23:07.172 --> 00:23:10.539
She's right about one thing.
We can't stay here.

00:23:10.573 --> 00:23:12.972
We've got to get out of here,
get to the roadhouse,

00:23:13.005 --> 00:23:14.539
Let people know
what's coming.

00:23:14.573 --> 00:23:15.872
That's a good point.

00:23:15.905 --> 00:23:18.005
"Night of the living dead"
didn't exactly end pretty.

00:23:18.039 --> 00:23:21.406
Lots of folks
up here are good with rifles.

00:23:21.439 --> 00:23:24.239
Even with all your hardware,
we're easy targets.

00:23:24.272 --> 00:23:28.372
So, unless you've got
some explosives...

00:23:32.905 --> 00:23:34.805
we could make some.

00:23:40.072 --> 00:23:42.339
Duane:
let me in, please!

00:23:43.239 --> 00:23:45.772
It's duane tanner.

00:23:49.439 --> 00:23:51.072
Oh, thank god.

00:23:57.039 --> 00:23:59.339
Duane, you okay?

00:23:59.372 --> 00:24:02.339
That's the guy that i...

00:24:02.372 --> 00:24:03.672
yeah.

00:24:03.705 --> 00:24:04.939
Who else is in here?

00:24:04.972 --> 00:24:07.439
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Easy there, chief.

00:24:07.473 --> 00:24:10.872
Hey, doc, give duane
a good once-Over, would you?

00:24:13.039 --> 00:24:15.339
Pam?

00:24:15.372 --> 00:24:16.506
Who are you?

00:24:16.539 --> 00:24:18.905
Never mind who i am.
Doc.

00:24:18.939 --> 00:24:21.239
Yeah, okay.

00:24:21.272 --> 00:24:22.805
Duane, where you been?

00:24:22.839 --> 00:24:24.972
I was on a fishing trip
up by roslyn.

00:24:25.005 --> 00:24:26.638
I came back
this afternoon.

00:24:26.672 --> 00:24:29.306
I saw roger mcgill being dragged
out of his house

00:24:29.339 --> 00:24:31.039
By people we know.

00:24:31.072 --> 00:24:33.473
They started cutting him
with knives.

00:24:33.506 --> 00:24:36.439
I ran. I've been hiding
in the woods ever since.

00:24:36.473 --> 00:24:38.072
Has anybody
seen my mom and dad?

00:24:38.106 --> 00:24:41.272
Awkward.

00:24:42.939 --> 00:24:45.738
You're bleeding.

00:24:47.672 --> 00:24:49.239
Where did you get that?

00:24:49.272 --> 00:24:50.972
I was running.
I must have tripped.

00:24:51.005 --> 00:24:54.239
Tie him up.
There's rope in there.

00:24:54.272 --> 00:24:55.839
Wait --
Sit down!

00:24:57.106 --> 00:25:00.005
Sorry, duane. He's right.
We've got to be careful.

00:25:00.039 --> 00:25:02.206
Careful? About what?

00:25:02.239 --> 00:25:03.506
Did they bleed on you?

00:25:03.539 --> 00:25:05.005
No.
What the hell?! No!

00:25:05.039 --> 00:25:08.005
Doc, any way to know for sure?
Any test?

00:25:08.039 --> 00:25:10.086
I've studied beverly's blood
work backwards and forwards.

00:25:10.086 --> 00:25:12.037
??

00:25:12.037 --> 00:25:14.538
It took three hours
for the virus to incubate.

00:25:14.538 --> 00:25:16.571
Sulfur didn't appear
in the blood until then,

00:25:16.605 --> 00:25:18.905
So, no, there would be
no way of knowing.

00:25:18.938 --> 00:25:22.805
Not until
after duane...turns.

00:25:22.838 --> 00:25:26.339
Dean, i've got to talk
to you. Now.

00:25:28.504 --> 00:25:30.438
Sit in that chair
over there.

00:25:32.538 --> 00:25:36.371
This is my vision, dean.
It's happening.

00:25:36.404 --> 00:25:37.671
Yeah, i figured.

00:25:37.705 --> 00:25:39.138
You can't kill him.
Not yet.

00:25:39.172 --> 00:25:41.038
We don't know
if he's infected or not.

00:25:41.072 --> 00:25:42.538
I think
we're pretty damn sure.

00:25:42.571 --> 00:25:44.538
Guy shows up out of nowhere,
cut on his leg,

00:25:44.571 --> 00:25:45.872
His whole family
is infected.

00:25:45.905 --> 00:25:47.780
We should keep him tied up,
and we should wait and see.

00:25:47.780 --> 00:25:50.671
For him to hulk out,
infect somebody else?

00:25:50.705 --> 00:25:52.438
No, thanks.
Can't take that chance.

00:25:53.872 --> 00:25:55.605
Look, man.
I'm not happy about this,

00:25:55.638 --> 00:25:57.504
But it's a tough job,
and you know that.

00:25:57.538 --> 00:25:58.738
It's supposed to be tough.

00:25:58.771 --> 00:26:01.776
We're supposed to struggle
with this.

00:26:01.776 --> 00:26:01.837
What does that buy us?

00:26:01.838 --> 00:26:03.972
A clear conscience,
for one.

00:26:04.005 --> 00:26:05.072
It's too late for that.

00:26:05.105 --> 00:26:07.404
What the hell
has happened to you?

00:26:07.438 --> 00:26:10.872
You might kill an innocent man,
and you don't even care.

00:26:10.905 --> 00:26:12.671
You don't act
like yourself anymore.

00:26:12.705 --> 00:26:16.605
You're acting like
one of those things out there.

00:26:19.438 --> 00:26:20.705
Hey.

00:26:22.371 --> 00:26:24.005
Open the damn door.

00:26:24.038 --> 00:26:25.838
Dean!

00:26:25.872 --> 00:26:29.205
Don't do it, dean!
Don't!

00:26:38.538 --> 00:26:41.239
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:26:41.272 --> 00:26:45.771
No, no, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:26:45.805 --> 00:26:47.605
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:26:47.638 --> 00:26:49.205
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:26:49.239 --> 00:26:51.838
No, he's not him --
Not anymore.

00:26:51.872 --> 00:26:56.239
Ask her! Ask the doctor!
It's not in me!

00:26:56.272 --> 00:26:58.805
I...just...

00:26:59.738 --> 00:27:00.905
i can't tell.

00:27:03.272 --> 00:27:05.272
Please, don't.

00:27:05.305 --> 00:27:08.105
Don't, please.
I swear it's not in me.

00:27:08.138 --> 00:27:14.214
It's not in me, i swear.
I swear, it's not in me.

00:27:14.538 --> 00:27:16.205
I've got no choice.

00:27:44.938 --> 00:27:46.504
Damn it.

00:28:12.571 --> 00:28:14.538
It's been
over four hours.

00:28:14.571 --> 00:28:16.038
Duane's blood
is still clean.

00:28:16.072 --> 00:28:18.538
I don't think
he's infected.

00:28:18.571 --> 00:28:21.571
I'd like to untie him,
if that's all right.

00:28:28.571 --> 00:28:31.205
Sure. Yeah.

00:28:37.305 --> 00:28:39.705
You know
i'm gonna ask you why.

00:28:39.738 --> 00:28:43.538
Yeah, i know.

00:28:43.571 --> 00:28:46.605
So, why?
Why didn't you do it?

00:28:50.671 --> 00:28:52.172
We need more alcohol.

00:28:58.872 --> 00:29:01.471
How are you holding up,
pam?

00:29:01.504 --> 00:29:05.172
Good.
It will all be over soon.

00:29:12.072 --> 00:29:16.172
In fact...

00:29:16.205 --> 00:29:18.671
i've been waiting
for this the whole time.

00:29:18.705 --> 00:29:20.005
For what?

00:29:20.038 --> 00:29:22.205
To get you alone.

00:29:22.239 --> 00:29:23.504
Aah!

00:29:53.571 --> 00:29:55.371
She bled on him.

00:29:57.305 --> 00:29:59.371
He's got the virus.

00:30:14.574 --> 00:30:17.116
Doctor, check his wound again,
would you?

00:30:23.167 --> 00:30:25.497
What does she need to
examine him for?

00:30:25.497 --> 00:30:27.726
You saw what happened.

00:30:27.726 --> 00:30:29.715
Did her blood
actually enter your wound?

00:30:29.715 --> 00:30:30.913
Come on,
of course it did!

00:30:30.914 --> 00:30:33.981
We can't take a chance.
You know what we have to do.

00:30:34.015 --> 00:30:35.515
Nobody is shooting
my brother.

00:30:35.548 --> 00:30:37.781
He's not gonna be
your brother much longer.

00:30:37.814 --> 00:30:40.348
Nobody's shooting anyone.
You were gonna shoot me!

00:30:40.382 --> 00:30:42.048
I still might.

00:30:42.081 --> 00:30:43.682
Dean, they're right.
I'm infected.

00:30:43.715 --> 00:30:46.148
Just give me the gun,
and i'll do it myself.

00:30:46.181 --> 00:30:48.649
Dean, i'm not gonna
become one of those things.

00:30:48.682 --> 00:30:49.948
We've still
got some time.

00:30:49.981 --> 00:30:51.181
Time for what?

00:30:51.215 --> 00:30:53.448
I understand he's your brother,
and i'm sorry.

00:30:53.482 --> 00:30:54.614
But i've got to take care
of this.

00:30:54.614 --> 00:30:57.520
You make a move, you'll be dead
before you hit the ground.

00:30:57.520 --> 00:30:59.386
Do i make myself clear?

00:30:59.387 --> 00:31:00.620
What are we
supposed to do?!

00:31:10.653 --> 00:31:13.086
Get the hell out of here.
That's what.

00:31:14.086 --> 00:31:18.003
Take my car.
You've got the explosives.

00:31:18.003 --> 00:31:20.836
There's an arsenal in there.
You two go with him.

00:31:20.870 --> 00:31:22.603
You got enough firepower
to handle anything now.

00:31:22.603 --> 00:31:23.870
What about you?

00:31:26.037 --> 00:31:29.271
Sam: dean, no.

00:31:29.304 --> 00:31:30.971
No.

00:31:31.004 --> 00:31:33.137
Go with them.
This is your only chance.

00:31:33.171 --> 00:31:35.971
You're not gonna
get rid of me that easy.

00:31:36.004 --> 00:31:38.503
No, he's right, man.
Come with us.

00:31:46.171 --> 00:31:47.804
Okay, it's your funeral.

00:31:54.304 --> 00:31:58.304
I'm sorry. Thanks for
everything, marshals.

00:31:58.338 --> 00:32:01.137
Oh, actually,
we're not really marshals.

00:32:01.171 --> 00:32:04.570
Um...oh.

00:32:22.570 --> 00:32:25.204
I wish
we had a deck of cards

00:32:25.237 --> 00:32:27.204
Or a foosball table
or something.

00:32:29.804 --> 00:32:33.470
Dean, don't do this.

00:32:33.503 --> 00:32:37.204
Just get the hell out
of here.

00:32:37.237 --> 00:32:39.071
No way.

00:32:43.704 --> 00:32:47.171
Give me my gun and leave.

00:32:47.204 --> 00:32:53.004
For the last time,
sam, no.

00:32:56.537 --> 00:33:00.171
This is the dumbest thing
you've ever done.

00:33:00.204 --> 00:33:02.503
I don't know about that.

00:33:02.537 --> 00:33:05.837
Remember that waitress
in tampa?

00:33:07.804 --> 00:33:12.438
Dean, i'm sick.
It's over for me.

00:33:12.470 --> 00:33:14.937
It doesn't have to be
for you.

00:33:14.971 --> 00:33:16.904
No, you can keep going.

00:33:16.937 --> 00:33:19.171
Who says i want to?

00:33:20.271 --> 00:33:22.104
What?

00:33:31.804 --> 00:33:33.137
I'm tired, sam.

00:33:34.204 --> 00:33:37.137
I'm tired of this job...

00:33:37.171 --> 00:33:39.704
this life...

00:33:39.737 --> 00:33:42.004
this weight
on my shoulders, man.

00:33:42.037 --> 00:33:43.237
I'm tired of it.

00:33:43.271 --> 00:33:45.737
So, what?
So, you're just gonna give up?

00:33:45.770 --> 00:33:47.904
I mean, you're just
gonna lay down and die?

00:33:47.937 --> 00:33:50.304
Look, dean, i know this stuff
with dad had --

00:33:50.338 --> 00:33:52.237
You're wrong.

00:33:53.770 --> 00:33:57.071
It's not about dad.

00:33:57.104 --> 00:33:59.204
I mean,
part of it is, sure --

00:33:59.237 --> 00:34:01.104
Then, what is it about?

00:34:17.804 --> 00:34:19.071
You better
come see this.

00:34:38.670 --> 00:34:41.637
There's no one.
Not anywhere.

00:34:41.670 --> 00:34:45.704
They've all
just vanished.

00:34:59.304 --> 00:35:01.603
Well,
it's been five hours,

00:35:01.637 --> 00:35:03.438
And your blood's
still clean.

00:35:03.470 --> 00:35:05.837
I don't understand it,
but i think you dodged a bullet.

00:35:05.870 --> 00:35:09.204
But i was exposed.
How could i not be infected?

00:35:09.237 --> 00:35:11.837
I don't know,
but you're just not.

00:35:11.870 --> 00:35:15.237
I mean, when you compare it
with the tanner samples --

00:35:15.271 --> 00:35:16.271
What the hell?

00:35:16.304 --> 00:35:18.904
What?

00:35:18.937 --> 00:35:23.503
Their blood --
There's no trace of the virus.

00:35:23.537 --> 00:35:26.438
No sulfur. Nothing.

00:35:34.770 --> 00:35:38.071
The sarge and i are
getting the hell out of here.

00:35:38.104 --> 00:35:40.404
Heading south.
You should come.

00:35:40.438 --> 00:35:42.071
I'd better get over
to sidewinder,

00:35:42.104 --> 00:35:43.503
Get the authorities
up here.

00:35:43.537 --> 00:35:47.004
If they'll believe me.

00:35:47.037 --> 00:35:48.603
Take care.

00:35:49.937 --> 00:35:52.171
What about him?

00:35:52.204 --> 00:35:56.104
He's gonna be fine.
No signs of infection.

00:36:08.770 --> 00:36:12.737
Hey, man, don't look at me.
I've got no clue.

00:36:12.770 --> 00:36:14.904
I swear, i'm gonna lose sleep
over this one.

00:36:14.937 --> 00:36:16.570
I mean, why here?
Why now?

00:36:16.603 --> 00:36:18.171
Where the hell
did everybody go?

00:36:18.204 --> 00:36:20.104
It's not like
they just freaking melted.

00:36:20.137 --> 00:36:23.037
Why was i immune?

00:36:23.071 --> 00:36:25.904
Yeah, you know what?
That's a good question.

00:36:25.937 --> 00:36:27.737
You know, i'm already
starting to feel

00:36:27.770 --> 00:36:30.104
Like this is the one
that got away.

00:36:59.037 --> 00:37:04.137
Do you mind pulling over
up ahead there?

00:37:04.171 --> 00:37:05.704
All right.

00:37:13.271 --> 00:37:14.971
I've got to make a call.

00:37:15.004 --> 00:37:16.438
No phone out here.

00:37:16.470 --> 00:37:18.570
I got it covered.

00:37:18.603 --> 00:37:20.371
What the hell is that?

00:37:47.737 --> 00:37:50.837
It's over.
You'll be pleased.

00:37:50.870 --> 00:37:55.438
I don't think any more tests
are necessary.

00:37:55.470 --> 00:38:00.804
The winchester boy --
Definitely immune as expected.

00:38:00.837 --> 00:38:05.971
Yes, of course.
Nothing left behind.

00:38:37.547 --> 00:38:40.847
So, last night --
You want to tell me

00:38:40.881 --> 00:38:43.847
What the hell
you were talking about?

00:38:43.881 --> 00:38:45.181
What do you mean?

00:38:45.214 --> 00:38:46.415
What do i mean?

00:38:46.447 --> 00:38:48.893
I mean you said
you were tired of the job

00:38:48.893 --> 00:38:51.113
And that it wasn't
just because of dad.

00:38:51.113 --> 00:38:52.124
Forget it.

00:38:52.124 --> 00:38:54.090
No, i can't.
No way.

00:38:54.091 --> 00:38:55.558
I thought
we were both gonna die.

00:38:55.592 --> 00:38:56.925
You can't hold that
over me.

00:38:56.959 --> 00:38:58.625
You can't pull that crap
with me, man.

00:38:58.658 --> 00:38:59.625
You're talking.

00:38:59.658 --> 00:39:01.124
And what if i don't?

00:39:01.158 --> 00:39:04.124
Then i guess i'll just have to
keep asking you

00:39:04.158 --> 00:39:05.291
Till you do.

00:39:11.158 --> 00:39:13.291
I don't know, man.

00:39:13.325 --> 00:39:15.825
I just think
maybe we ought to...

00:39:18.825 --> 00:39:21.158
...go to the grand canyon.

00:39:23.158 --> 00:39:25.024
What?

00:39:25.058 --> 00:39:26.492
Yeah, you know,
all this driving

00:39:26.525 --> 00:39:28.124
Back and forth
across the country --

00:39:28.158 --> 00:39:30.291
Do you know i've never
been to the grand canyon?

00:39:30.325 --> 00:39:32.258
Or we could go to t.J.
Or hollywood --

00:39:32.291 --> 00:39:34.158
See if we could
bang lindsay lohan.

00:39:34.191 --> 00:39:36.091
You're not
making any sense.

00:39:36.124 --> 00:39:39.758
I just think we should
take a break from all this.

00:39:39.792 --> 00:39:42.258
Why do we got to get stuck
with all the responsibility?

00:39:42.291 --> 00:39:44.925
Why can't
we live life a little bit?

00:39:44.959 --> 00:39:46.658
Why are you
saying all this?

00:39:49.658 --> 00:39:51.458
No, no, no, no, no.

00:39:51.492 --> 00:39:54.124
Dean, you're my brother,
all right?

00:39:54.158 --> 00:39:56.758
So, whatever weight
you're carrying,

00:39:56.792 --> 00:39:58.258
Let me help
a little bit.

00:40:02.358 --> 00:40:05.658
I can't.
I promised.

00:40:05.692 --> 00:40:06.892
Who?

00:40:06.925 --> 00:40:09.091
Dad.

00:40:11.191 --> 00:40:13.625
What are you
talking about?

00:40:14.892 --> 00:40:20.358
Right before dad died...
he told me something.

00:40:22.625 --> 00:40:24.959
He told me something
about you.

00:40:28.058 --> 00:40:30.058
What?

00:40:32.225 --> 00:40:35.558
Dean,
what did he tell you?

00:40:40.058 --> 00:40:43.024
